  === KEY LEARNING ===

  L8. BREAKEVEN RATCHET IS UNIVERSALLY POSITIVE
      Unlike other overlays that are portfolio-composition-dependent (L2),
      breakeven works for EVERY strategy and EVERY combination tested.
      It has zero negative interactions because it only converts losers
      to scratch — never reduces the upside of winners. This makes it
      the only exit improvement that should be DEFAULT-ON for all strategies.

  L9. RANKINGS SHOW STRATEGY-PERIOD DIVERGENCE
      All-time best (4-edge-conv) ≠ recent best (s60). Rankings shift
      dramatically across timeframes. Implication: portfolio allocation
      should weight recent performance more than all-time, or use
      regime-adaptive allocation (dynamic weights already doing this).

  L10. FLAT TIGHT TRAIL BEATS PROGRESSIVE SCHEDULE
       Progressive trail schedule [[0,3.0],[1,2.5],[2,2.0],[3,1.5]] was
       optimized for trending markets but too loose overall. Flat 1.5 ATR
       trail captures profits faster across ALL regimes. Key insight:
       the "let winners run" philosophy costs more than it gains — most
       crypto trades don't trend far enough to justify wide trails.
       20/24 strategies BETTER, 0 WORSE at all-time horizon.

  L11. SHARED STRATEGIES BLOCK PORTFOLIO-SPECIFIC EXITS
       bear_target_mult=3.0 helps 4-edge+ptp but HURTS s58/s60/4-edge
       because the same strategy files (s57, s63, s65) are shared across
       portfolios. Exit params must be universally beneficial or not deployed.
       Exception: s80/s81 are ONLY in s80+s81 pools, so bear_max_hold=12
       can be added safely to those specific strategies.

  L12. REGIME-ADAPTIVE EXITS REJECTED
       Tested in v3 ablation (16 configs). Thin margins, inconsistent crash
       resistance, added complexity. Current simple exit stack (flat trail
       + breakeven + regime exit) is at a local optimum. Don't add more
       conditional logic — the marginal benefit is zero or negative.

